09:17-09:41 a DeepSeek V4 Flash vLLM stack (another recipe, root's compose project, relaunched by a cron scheduler every few minutes while 8888 was down) held both GPUs; removed for good at 09:41 (containers, images, units, launch directory).
09:42-09:47 with the GPUs free, two more starts failed the same way: rank 1 (worker) ibv_reg_mr_iova2 'Cannot allocate memory' at NCCL's first registration (transport setup, sendProxyConnect), the head fine; a host-side perftest (ib_write_bw, head -> worker, 1 MiB) ran at 109 Gb/s, so the NIC and RDMA were up.
09:47 the worker still held 34 GB of page cache the per-start drop_caches had not released (the 25 GB image load at 08:55) and far fewer high-order free pages than the head (/proc/buddyinfo order-10+: 1760/1379/614 vs 2807/1395/270 at order 11-13 but 83999 vs 12958 order-0 pages free); 'sync; drop_caches; compact_memory' on the worker, then the next start came up first time. Likely cause: the mlx5 driver could not get the kernel pages it needs for a memory region on a fragmented worker; run.sh now compacts after it drops caches.

